<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pablo Escobar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1949">1949</a>–<a href="/years/1993">1993</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pablo Escobar was a Colombian drug lord who led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medellin-cartel">Medellín Cartel</a>, which supplied most of the cocaine smuggled into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> in the 1980s. He won popularity in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medellin">Medellín</a> through housing projects and briefly sat in Congress, but waged a war of bombings and murders against the state to avoid extradition. He was shot dead by Colombian police in Medellín in December 1993.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pablo-escobar.jpg" alt="Pablo Escobar" width="320" height="415" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Colombian National Police · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pablo_Escobar_Mug_(cropped)(b).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
